; Export list for the cdylib, which is the in-process activation server.
;
; Rust already exports these through `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`, so this file is
; not what makes them reachable — `PRIVATE` is. Without it MSVC warns LNK4104
; on each one: these names are only ever reached by `GetProcAddress` from the
; COM and WinRT loaders, never linked against, so putting them in the
; generated import library would invite a caller to bind to them statically.
; `PRIVATE` keeps them in the DLL's export table and out of the .lib.
;
; Listing a name here does not restrict the export table — `no_mangle` alone
; is enough to be exported, which is why `DllGetActivationFactory` was
; reachable for a while without appearing here. It is listed now so it gets
; the same `PRIVATE` treatment as the rest.
;
; Self-registration (`DllRegisterServer` / `DllUnregisterServer`) was removed
; on 2026-11-09; src/comio/activation.rs has the reasoning. `DllCanUnloadNow`
; went with it and came back the same day, this time answering from a real
; count of what is live -- see src/comio/unload.rs.
EXPORTS
    DllGetActivationFactory PRIVATE
    DllGetClassObject       PRIVATE
    DllCanUnloadNow         PRIVATE
